AWS S3 CLI Commands Every DevOps Engineer Should Know
Managing Amazon Simple Storage Service using AWS Command Line Interface makes cloud operations faster and easier. ☁️
✅ Common AWS S3 CLI Commands
📌 List all S3 buckets

aws s3 ls

📌 Create a new bucket

aws s3 mb s3://my-demo-bucket

📌 Upload file to S3

aws s3 cp file.txt s3://my-demo-bucket

📌 Download file from S3

aws s3 cp s3://my-demo-bucket/file.txt .

📌 Sync local folder with S3

aws s3 sync ./website s3://my-demo-bucket

📌 Remove file from S3

aws s3 rm s3://my-demo-bucket/file.txt

💡 Why Use AWS CLI?
✔ Faster resource management
 ✔ Easy automation
 ✔ Useful in CI/CD pipelines
 ✔ Saves time for DevOps Engineers
Learning CLI commands is one of the best ways to improve cloud and automation skills. 🚀
